WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.100
-Welcome to the show. Thank you
so much for being here.

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.200
I appreciate it.
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.267
-Yeah, this is a big --

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:08.968
a big weekend for you,
which is interesting to me.

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:10.200
I did not know this.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.467
Your goddaughter hosted
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:14.968
-Yes, she did! Zozo.
-Zoe Kravitz is your...

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:16.267
-Zoe Kravitz. Yeah.
-...is your goddaughter.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:17.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:19.200
-Mm-hmm. She killed it.
She killed it.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.767
-She was fantastic.
-Yeah.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:22.534
-We have a picture
of you and --

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.701
This is you and Lisa
and Baby Zoe.

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:26.767
-Oh, yeah. Well, you can't
really tell it's her, though.

00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:28.868
-No, you can't tell.
Yeah, that's Zoe right there.

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:30.300
-Take our word.
-Exactly, yeah.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.868
-And why I'm wearing a towel
on my head, I do not know.

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:33.501
-Yeah.
-I must've been chilly.

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:35.601
-Is this from, like,
"A Different World"?

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:36.901
Is that where you met?
-Yeah.

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:38.934
Well, we met before
"A Different World," actually.

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:41.100
-Oh, you did? So you've
been friends for a while.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.067
-Yeah, we met in -- Yeah, in --
like, an acting workshop.

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:46.567
-Did Zoe ask for any advice
on how to host?

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:47.868
You've hosted
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:50.434
-I did, many moons ago.

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:51.868
And she doesn't need any advice.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:53.334
She's got it.
-She's just so cool.

00:00:53.334 --> 00:00:55.968
-I mean, I was there
to cheer her on, of course.

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:57.200
-I ask her advice on anything.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.634
I'm like, "Zoe,
just tell me how to be cool."

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.300
-I ask her for advice.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.901
-It's the other way around.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.767
-I saw that yesterday marked
the 30th anniversary of

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:08.601
"My Cousin Vinny," which is --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:12.367
One of your great films
that we all love.

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:14.100
When you're doing that --
When you do that movie,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.767
when you were filming it,
did you have any idea

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:19.701
it would be that big of a hit
or that you would win an Oscar?

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:22.868
-No. [ Laughs ] I was just happy
to have a job.

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:24.767
-[ Laughter ]
-I don't know.

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.200
Who is the person who thinks,
"I'm going to win an Oscar"?

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.501
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:28.501 --> 00:01:30.734
-What kind of cajones
are you walking around with?

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:34.834
-Yeah, exactly. But it became
the biggest movie ever.

00:01:34.834 --> 00:01:36.934
I mean, I think Vice President
Kamala Harris

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:38.601
said that
that's her favorite movie.

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:39.868
-Kamala Harris said that?
-Yes.

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.000
That's her favorite movie.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.601
"My Cousin Vinny." Loves it.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:45.934
They teach it in colleges --
in law-school classes.

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:48.234
-That I knew. That part I knew.
Yes, a lot of --

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:53.167
Many a lawyer have kind of
used that line on me.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.734
-Did they ever ask you
come in and, like, speak?

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:56.267
-They ask me
to come in and speak.

00:01:56.267 --> 00:02:00.100
They ask me other things.
-Yeah, that's wild. Yeah, yeah.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.968
-[ Laughter ]
-You've been -- You've been --

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:04.167
You've won and you've been
nominated for many, many awards.

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:07.000
But there is an honor that
I'm not sure if you know about.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.133
There's a sandwich
named after you.

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:11.133
The world-famous
Lioni's deli in Brooklyn.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:12.434
-Oh, really?
-The Marisa Tomei.

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:13.501
-I don't know that.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.167
-Well, it's a very
exclusive club.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:17.934
-[ Laughter ]
-So, on the sandwich is --

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:19.200
tell me if you like this --

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.767
fried eggplant.
-I like it.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.234
-Fresh mozzarella.
-Love it.

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:23.734
-Bread crumbs.
-Love it.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:26.534
-And mushroom stuffing.

00:02:26.534 --> 00:02:30.200
-Not in a sandwich. Ohh.
-No mushroom stuffing?

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.734
-I'm disappointing
the Lioni's crew, I guess.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.834
-No. Not a mushroom fan?

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:35.868
-Well, I like --
What about yourself?

00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:38.467
-I do not like mushrooms.
I don't like mayonnaise, either.

00:02:38.467 --> 00:02:40.267
-Oh, yeah...palate.

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:41.801
-Mushrooms and mayonnaise,
that's the only thing I don't --

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:43.767
Yeah, I don't enjoy those. Yeah.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.701
Well, if we could
talk to those guys --

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:47.968
I figured
if you've never heard about it,

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:49.167
maybe you've never tried it.

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:51.067
I got one with
no mushrooms on it.

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:52.801
-Ohh.
-I got two of them actually.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:56.200
I figured you could try
your own Marisa Tomei

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.000
on "The Tonight Show."

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.133
Marisa Tomei eating
a Marisa Tomei.

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:01.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Okay.

00:03:01.901 --> 00:03:04.200
♪♪

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.234
Do you have napkins for us
and everything?

00:03:06.234 --> 00:03:07.801
Do we have a napkin?
-Oh, I do.

00:03:07.801 --> 00:03:09.400
-I feel like this
is going to be awkward.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.801
-[ Muffled ] No...

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:12.300
Yes!

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.400
♪♪

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.434
That's fan-- What do you think?

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:21.601
-I have to lean over
with a sandwich this big.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.434
I, like, can't do it,
like, right here.

00:03:23.434 --> 00:03:24.767
I'm gonna make a mess.

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:27.267
-No, you can barely even talk
when you have a bite.

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:29.334
Can we talk about
"Spider-Man: No Way Home"?

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.234
-Yes. Yeah.
-You were fantastic in this.

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:32.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:37.400
Really -- You're always --
You're great in all of them.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.267
It's made almost -- I know.

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:42.100
It made almost $2 billion
worldwide.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.634
I mean, it is a giant movie.

00:03:43.634 --> 00:03:46.067
It's the third-highest
grossing movie in history.

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:47.467
-It's so cool. It's so cool.

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:48.901
It's really a cool thing
to be a part of.

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
-But it's a great movie, too.

00:03:50.234 --> 00:03:52.701
I loved every single
second of it.

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:55.667
You play May Parker.
I love -- I love you.

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:58.200
I love Tom Holland.
I love Zendaya.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:01.067
I couldn't get enough of every
single person in this movie.

00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:02.767
I go, "I don't want it to end.

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:04.701
I want it to just keep
going on and on."

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:06.434
Is it tough to do those movies

00:04:06.434 --> 00:04:09.801
knowing that you can't spoil
anything or talk about anything?

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:13.200
-Well, yes, at first it is,
because you have to sign

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:16.234
a lot of things
and it's all under secrecy.

00:04:16.234 --> 00:04:17.467
Friends will ask.

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:18.901
Or family members
will ask about it.

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:21.234
-So you're happy it's out.
-I'm happy it's out.

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:22.534
I'm happy it's out now.

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:24.534
And I don't have to keep
that secret anymore.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.100
-Yeah.
I mean, I wouldn't bother you

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:28.100
with questions, like,
if I saw you on the street.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.334
-You wouldn't?

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:30.634
-No.
I'd just be like, "I'm cool."

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.367
-Would you just like --
-I wouldn't do it.

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:33.968
Because I already know
the thing.

00:04:33.968 --> 00:04:36.234
The answer is, "Jimmy,
don't make me do this," yeah.

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:37.667
So I wouldn't do it.

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.801
And then after seeing it,
wow, there's some spoilers.

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:41.901
-There are some spoilers.
Yes. Yeah.

00:04:41.901 --> 00:04:43.968
But maybe a few people
don't know yet.

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:46.968
So we can't --
we still can't talk about it.

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:49.133
-We still can't t-- Yeah.
Can we not talk about --

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:51.033
-Mnh-mnh-mnh-mnh-mnh-mnh-mnh!

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:53.901
-Can we talk about the --
-We can talk about mnh-mnh --

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:56.367
-Can we talk about that?
-Yeah, we can talk about that.

00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:58.067
-We can?
-If we want to.

00:04:58.067 --> 00:04:59.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:03.267
I have no idea
what he's talking about.

00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:07.267
-The fact that
there is a multiverse.

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:08.667
-Oh, yes.
There is a multiverse.

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:10.033
-Okay. We can say that.
-Yes.

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:12.133
-Yeah, I don't want to ruin it
for any fans out there.

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:13.167
-Right, yes.
There is a multiverse.

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:14.467
-If you haven't been
to the movies --

00:05:14.467 --> 00:05:16.200
-That was part of the secrecy,
though. That's true.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.334
That was part of the secrecy
originally.

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:19.767
Now a lot of people know.
-Yeah.

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:21.400
But the thing was,
if anyone asked me about it,

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:22.834
I would have nothing --

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:25.634
I don't understand
the multiverse, myself.

00:05:25.634 --> 00:05:27.601
-[ Laughter ]
-So you couldn't spoil it.

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:29.634
You'd be like,
"I don't know what it is."

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:30.968
-Our wonderful director, Jon,
and I'm like,

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:33.067
"And so where am I now?

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:35.100
Okay, well, can you explain it
to me one more time?"

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.367
-[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:36.367 --> 00:05:38.234
Well, knowing that
there is a multiverse --

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:40.234
-Yeah, what do you think --
Are you done with the sandwich?

00:05:40.234 --> 00:05:42.067
-[ Laughter ]
-No, I can go for it.

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:43.601
I actually really --

00:05:43.601 --> 00:05:44.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:47.901
♪♪

00:05:47.901 --> 00:05:49.601
Now...

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:51.400
[ Muffled ]
Now...multiverse...

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:56.200
[ Both mumbling ]

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.367
-Yeah.

00:05:57.367 --> 00:05:58.834
-Do you think that --

00:05:58.834 --> 00:06:02.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:05.234
Do you think
that you would ever do --

00:06:05.234 --> 00:06:07.734
Would May Parker be
in a multiverse thing?

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:10.067
Would you ever want
to do something with --

00:06:10.067 --> 00:06:11.367
-Yeah, I would love to come back

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:13.767
and be part of that --
I want to be --

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:15.167
-Like, a different movie?

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:16.300
-Yeah.
-You would do it?

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:17.667
-Yeah.
There's history there, too.

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:20.367
May Parker hooks up
with Ant-Man in one of --

00:06:20.367 --> 00:06:22.100
Well, I mean, she's
a stand-alone character,

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.868
of course.
-Yes, of course.

00:06:23.868 --> 00:06:26.901
-But there are more avenues
to explore.

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:28.567
-All right. I'm going to
root for that right now.

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:30.534
-Is there anything in my teeth?

00:06:30.534 --> 00:06:32.601
-Let me see. I will tell you.
No, you look beautiful.

00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:34.334
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:34.334 --> 00:06:36.267
Here's Marisa Tomei,
not the sandwich,

00:06:36.267 --> 00:06:37.968
"Spider-Man: No Way Home."

00:06:37.968 --> 00:06:39.167
Take a look.

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:40.334
-I just feel so dumb.

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:42.000
I didn't realize
you were miserable.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.400
-No, it was really fun.
That's why --

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.701
You know,
that's why they call it a fling.

00:06:45.701 --> 00:06:47.300
And we flung.
-It was fun.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.667
I could have been more fun.

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:50.667
I can be fun.
-We'll hang out again.

00:06:50.667 --> 00:06:52.067
-Wait. When do you think?

00:06:52.067 --> 00:06:54.534
[ Objects clattering ]

00:06:54.534 --> 00:06:55.834
I should see what that is.

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:57.834
-No. No, no, no, no.
-This is what I do.

00:06:57.834 --> 00:06:59.400
-He's always coming and going.
It's not --

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:00.334
-Peter.
-Oh, no.

00:07:00.334 --> 00:07:01.300
-Oh, God.
-Oh, no.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:02.767
-Peter?
-I don't know what to do!

00:07:02.767 --> 00:07:04.167
-Peter!

00:07:04.167 --> 00:07:06.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Marisa Tomei, everybody!

00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:08.901
"Spider-Man: No Way Home"

00:07:08.901 --> 00:07:11.300
is available on digital
starting tomorrow.

